      "commit": {
        "parents": [
          {
            "commit": "40b80bc0485c7c651c33f67586c5e24b0bff061b",
            "subject": "LU-20867 gss: re-resolve lsvcgssd ioctl device on failure"
          }
        ],
        "author": {
          "name": "Patrick Farrell",
          "email": "patrick@thelustrecollective.com",
          "date": "2026-10-30 21:55:30.000000000",
          "tz": -300
        },
        "committer": {
          "name": "Patrickbot",
          "email": "patrick-bot@mulberrytree.us",
          "date": "2026-10-30 21:55:30.000000000",
          "tz": -300
        },
        "subject": "LU-20869 tests: batch pool_remove in destroy_pool_int",
        "message": "LU-20869 tests: batch pool_remove in destroy_pool_int\n\ndestroy_pool_int ran one lctl pool_remove per OST in the pool, and\neach call waits for the client to see the change. Teardown of a\n4 OST pool took about 7.2s on a test VM, mostly in those waits.\n\nPass the whole OST list to a single pool_remove, which the tool\nalready accepts. destroy_pool on a 4 OST pool drops from 7.2s\n(5 runs, 7.2 to 8.2s) to 3.9s (5 runs, 3.1 to 4.9s). The pool\nstill has to be seen empty on the MDS and gone on every MDT and\nthe client before destroy_pool returns, so nothing is checked\nless. The remaining time is config llog propagation, 1 to 2s per\nstep, which polling more often does not shorten.\n\nost-pools 1n 5a 5b 6 12 13 16 19 24 sum of test times, 3 runs\neach: 120, 124, 119s before; 147 (one unexplained 50s test 16),\n95, 93s after. A full ost-pools run destroys 46 pools and a full\nsanity-pfl run 11. At about 3.3s each that is roughly 150s and\n36s per run. With 5648 ost-pools and 4831 sanity-pfl runs per\n30 days, the expected saving is about 1.0M test seconds in CI.\n\nTest-Parameters: trivial testlist=ost-pools\nTest-Parameters: trivial testlist=sanity-pfl\nAssisted-by: ClaudeCode:claude-sonnet-5-5\nSigned-off-by: Patrick Farrell <patrick@thelustrecollective.com>\nChange-Id: Idca322f4a258f99235e9b844721e855a9e7f2a76\n"
      },
      "branch": "refs/heads/master"
    }
  },
